## 🧠 DOMAIN RULES

> **Highest-value section. Non-obvious rules that cause bugs when unknown.**
> **Only write what a senior developer would NOT figure out in 30 minutes of reading the code.**

- **MySQL on XAMPP**: Always port 3306, user `root`, no password, database `fondtracker`. Never assume a different config.
- **Bun executable path on this machine**: `C:\Users\Ruben\AppData\Local\Microsoft\WinGet\Packages\Oven-sh.Bun_Microsoft.Winget.Source_8wekyb3d8bbwe\bun-windows-x64\bun.exe`
- **Server must be killed by PID, not port**: `Get-NetTCPConnection -LocalPort 3741` returns System Idle Process (PID 0) which cannot be killed. Use `Get-Process -Name bun | Stop-Process -Force` instead.
- **Yahoo Finance only works for ETFs**: Mutual funds (`.BC` tickers, Spanish fund tickers) return zero historical data. Only ETFs with real exchange tickers (`.AS`, `.DE`, `.L`) have chart data. The `ticker` field on investments is nullable for this reason.
- **QueFondos fallback for mutual funds**: When Yahoo Finance returns no data for an ISIN-based ticker, `fetchYahooChart()` and `fetchCurrentPrice()` automatically fall back to `fetchQueFondosData(isin)` which scrapes www.quefondos.com for official NAV, historical monthly series, and 1Y/3Y/5Y returns. QueFondos data is marked with `dataSource: "quefondos"` and includes a `staleWarning` if >7 business days old.
- **ISIN auto-discovery**: When an investment has no ticker, `tryDiscoverTicker(isin)` first tries QueFondos (returns ISIN as ticker), then tries Yahoo with `.BC`, `.MC`, `.MA` suffixes. Discovered tickers are persisted to the `investments.ticker` column via `updateInvestmentTicker()`.
- **Fund metadata enrichment**: `getFundExtraMetadata(isin, category, name, returns)` in `src/server/metadata.ts` provides synthetic TER, sector allocation, geography, and top holdings data based on fund category/name heuristics (S&P 500, MSCI World, Spain equity, Europe, Mixto, generic). Returns are real when sourced from QueFondos, otherwise use sensible defaults.
- **Cross-source price verification**: Yahoo Finance prices are cross-checked against QueFondos NAV when both are available. `verifyFundData()` compares prices and produces a `verificationLog` string. Discrepancies >1% are flagged and QueFondos is preferred (it has official NAV).
- **fund_prices cache table**: `db.ts` creates a `fund_prices` table with `(isin, price, currency, updated_at)`. `setFundPrice()` is called after every successful price fetch. `getFundPrice()` serves as fallback when live fetch fails. This reduces API calls and survives restarts.
- **Fund catalog lives in MySQL, not in code**: The `fund_catalog` table is the single source of truth. `src/server/fund-catalog.ts` is OBSOLETE and unused by the server — it was the original hardcoded catalog before migration.
- **Settings table columns**: Named `setting_key`/`setting_value` (NOT `key`/`value`) to avoid MySQL reserved word conflicts. The `schema.sql` file has the old column names — always use `ensureSchema()` from `db.ts` as the truth.
- **investments.user_id**: Added via ALTER TABLE, not in original schema. Always check for column existence in `ensureSchema()` before assuming it exists.
- **All API routes except `/api/health`, `/api/funds/search`, `/api/funds/catalog/:isin`, `/api/funds/chart/:ticker` require JWT auth**. The `requireUser(req)` helper returns a `Response` (401) on failure — always check `if (user instanceof Response) return user;`.
- **JWT_SECRET has a dev default**: `fondtracker-dev-secret-change-in-prod`. MUST be overridden in production via env var.
- **Client is bundled to `dist/` by `build.ts`**: The build only bundles client-side code (HTML/JS/CSS for browser). The server runs directly from TypeScript source via `bun run src/server/index.ts`. Never try to run `dist/index.js` — it doesn't exist.
- **Server routing split**: `/` serves root `index.html` (static Tailwind CDN landing page). `/dashboard`, `/login`, `/register` serve the React SPA (imported as `index` from `../client/index.html`). `/*` falls through to root `index.html`. Never change `/` to serve the React SPA — the landing page CSS is incompatible with Tailwind v4.
- **Landing page is NOT React**: The root `index.html` is a standalone static page with Tailwind CDN v3. Auth detection is inline vanilla JS (not React). Do not import React components or Tailwind v4 utilities into this file.
- **Schema files are reference only**: `schema.sql` and `schema-settings-catalog.sql` are not applied automatically. The actual schema is managed by `ensureSchema()` in `db.ts` which runs on every server start.
- **WhatsApp Phone Numbers**: Extracted and isolated per user. A user's WhatsApp alerts are sent strictly to their own registered phone number stored in `users.phone`. A user's notification parameters do not default to global environment variables or fallbacks if a `userId` is supplied.
- **WhatsApp Formatting Limit**: Text notifications are optimized to fit within 26 characters of width under monospaced (```) formatting, avoiding wrapping on mobile WhatsApp screens. Performance lists use shortened layouts with 8-character bar graphics and 9-character fund names.

### Deprecated / Renamed
> **Anti-hallucination anchors. Never reach for these — use the replacement instead.**

| Dead symbol / API | Replaced by | Why |
|-------------------|-------------|-----|
| `fund-catalog.ts` functions (`getFundByIsin`, `searchFunds`) | `queries.searchFundCatalog()`, `queries.getFundCatalogByIsin()` in `db.ts` | Fund catalog moved from hardcoded array to MySQL. Server no longer imports from `fund-catalog.ts`. |
| `schema.sql` settings table (`key`, `value` columns) | `schema-settings-catalog.sql` (`setting_key`, `setting_value`) | MySQL reserved word conflict. Always use `setting_key`/`setting_value`. |
| `data/sentinel.db` (SQLite) | MySQL via `db.ts` pool | Project migrated from SQLite to MySQL/XAMPP. SQLite files are leftover artifacts. |
| `api.fetchChart` (old name) | `api.getChartData(ticker, range, interval)` | Renamed during refactor of api.ts with new YahooChartData type including QueFondos fields |
| `listInvestments` returning raw rows | `listInvestments` now with auto-ticker-discovery + price caching | Ticker resolution and price caching in fund_prices table added to the pipeline |

