## ✅ CODE QUALITY

> **Run this before every output. Mandatory. If any item fails, fix it first.**

- [x] Every function does one thing. If you can say "and", split it.
- [x] No function longer than ~30 lines. Extract helpers.
- [x] No nesting deeper than 3 levels. Use early returns to flatten.
- [x] No duplicated logic. Extract if the same block appears twice.
- [x] No hardcoded values (strings, numbers, URLs). Use constants or config.
- [x] No unused variables, imports, or parameters.
- [x] Error paths handled. No silent `catch (e) {}`.
- [x] New files placed in the correct directory per STRUCTURE MAP rules.
- [x] Pattern match: if this pattern exists elsewhere in the codebase, mirror it exactly.

### Forbidden — never produce this
- `eval()` or `Function()` constructor
- SQL strings built by concatenation (parameterized queries always)
- `innerHTML` with unsanitized data (use `textContent` or a sanitizer)
- Secrets or credentials in source code (use env vars)
- `any` type in TypeScript (use proper types)
- Mutable function arguments
- Boolean flags that change function behavior (`doThing(true)`) — use named options

