## 🗒 AI NOTES

> **Most valuable section. Append only. Newest first. Dated.**
> **Severity tags: `[!]` breaks if ignored · `[~]` non-obvious gotcha · `[?]` unresolved question**

`2026-07-17 [!] — WhatsApp settings and user phone parameters are fully isolated per user. No user configuration defaults to global environment variables or fallbacks if a userId is supplied.`

`2026-07-17 [~] — Landing page settings submenus in index.html toggle the display of the main content wrapper ('dropdown-main-content') to avoid overlapping/clipping of forms and buttons. The view size recalculates natively.`

`2026-07-12 [!] — investments table has user_id column added via ALTER TABLE, NOT in original schema.sql. ensureSchema() checks for it and adds it if missing. Do not assume it exists in schema.sql.`

`2026-07-12 [!] — fund-catalog.ts is OBSOLETE. The server no longer imports from it. All fund lookups go through MySQL fund_catalog table via db.ts queries. Do not add imports from fund-catalog.ts to any server file.`

`2026-07-12 [~] — Bun build (build.ts) only builds CLIENT code to dist/. Server runs from TypeScript source directly. Never try to run dist/index.js — it doesn't exist.`

`2026-07-12 [~] — The auth middleware pattern: requireUser(req) returns either {id, username} or a Response (401). Every protected route must check: const user = await requireUser(req); if (user instanceof Response) return user;`

`2026-07-12 [~] — CSS variables --color-profit and --color-loss are defined in styles.css @theme block. They were missing before the polish pass, causing profit/loss colors to render as default text color. Always verify custom CSS vars exist when adding new color references.`

`2026-07-12 [?] — CNMV (fondos.cnmv.es) website was unreachable via webfetch. Morningstar API screener returns 0 results for Spanish fund ISINs. Hansainvest API deprecated. Need alternative free data source for mutual fund data.`

`2026-07-12 [~] — Seed script (seed-funds.ts) uses INSERT IGNORE with batch inserts. Duplicate ISINs are silently skipped. This is intentional — running seed multiple times is safe.`

`2026-07-15 [!] — quefondos.ts fetches from www.quefondos.com with ISIN in query param. The page contains a `var fondo = [[...]]` JavaScript variable with monthly historical price data. If the page contains `{ISIN}` placeholder text, the fund is not found and `null` is returned. All callers in yahoo.ts handle null gracefully.`

`2026-07-15 [!] — metadata.ts uses heuristic matching (category/name contains keywords) to determine fund profile. It does NOT fetch real data from any source for sectors/geography/holdings — these are hardcoded templates per profile. Only returns (1Y/3Y/5Y) can be real (from QueFondos) or fallback defaults. TER values are sensible estimates per fund type.`
`2026-07-15 [~] — tryDiscoverTicker(isin) has a specific priority: QueFondos first (returns ISIN itself as ticker), then Yahoo with `.BC`, then `.MC`, then `.MA`. Once found, the ticker is persisted to the `investments.ticker` column so subsequent loads don't need to re-discover. This is critical for performance.`

`2026-07-15 [~] — getSpecificFundUrl() in api.ts has a complex fallback chain: 1) Ibercaja slug generation, 2) hardcoded ISIN-to-URL map, 3) ETF manager search portals (iShares, Vanguard, Amundi, Xtrackers), 4) Google search with `site:bankdomain.com + ISIN`, 5) QueFondos fallback for any ISIN, 6) Yahoo Finance for non-ISIN tickers.`

`2026-07-15 [~] — The fund_prices cache table is upserted on every successful price fetch. getFundPrice() is called as fallback when live fetch fails (network error, API timeout, etc.). This means prices can be up to N minutes stale (depending on last successful fetch), which is acceptable for a NAV-based tracker.`

`2026-07-15 [~] — Chart data auto-refreshes every 60 seconds in FundCard. ActiveTab state is maintained during refresh. Canvas chart with hover tooltip re-renders when `hoveredIndex` state changes — this is efficient because React only re-renders the specific path.`

`2026-07-15 [~] — The `/api/banks` endpoint returns a static map of bank names to official fund search URLs. This is defined inline in index.ts, not in a database table. To add/remove banks, edit the route handler directly.`

`2026-07-17 [!] — Landing page root index.html uses Tailwind CDN v3 (not v4 like the React SPA). CSS classes are incompatible between them. The React SPA (src/client/) uses Tailwind v4 syntax (bg-brand-primary/10) while the static landing uses Tailwind CDN v3 syntax (bg-brand-primary bg-opacity-10). Never mix these — the Tailwind config is in the root index.html <script> tag.`

`2026-07-17 [!] — The .sm-show CSS class on the username span requires !important to override the inline style="display:none" attribute. Without !important the class has no effect because inline styles beat class selectors in specificity. The class must be defined in the <style> tag at the top of root index.html.`

`2026-07-17 [!] — The Tailwind CDN config in root index.html uses important: '#app-root'. This means all Tailwind utilities (hidden, md:flex, etc.) generate selectors like #app-root .hidden. The body element has id="app-root". Do NOT add a custom .hidden { display: none !important } rule — it breaks responsive Tailwind classes like hidden md:flex that override it at breakpoint. Tailwind CDN provides its own .hidden class.`

`2026-07-17 [~] — Landing page auth settings dropdown uses subviews injected as child divs of #user-dropdown. Each subview has id="dd-subview". closeAllViews() removes the element. The gear button toggles the dropdown. Click outside closes both dropdown and subviews. All form operations (email change, password change, delete account) call PUT/DELETE /api/auth/me with Bearer token.`

`2026-07-17 [~] — Server route mapping for pages: / serves root index.html (static), /dashboard serves React SPA (index), /login and /register serve React SPA (index), /* falls through to root index.html. The React SPA import is at top of server: import index from "../client/index.html". Root index.html is served via Bun.file(join(PROJECT_ROOT, "index.html")).`

